{"file":"Cairn Verify — did the AI really fix it_-1.2.0-v1.zip","bytes":208837,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"cairn-verify","displayName":"Cairn Verify — did the AI really fix it?","description":"Checks what your coding agent said it did — fixed, tested, removed, wired, no behaviour change — against the repository, and gives each claim a verdict in plain words: holds, doesn't hold, or can't tell. Unsticks an agent going in circles by finding the live and dead copies it keeps confusing. Read-only, self-testing script.","version":"1.2.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/nicuk/did-ai-really-fix-it","homepage":"https://github.com/nicuk/did-ai-really-fix-it#readme","keywords":["code-review","ai-code-review","pr-review","verify","claims","ai-agent","vibe-coding","ai-built-apps","dead-code","tests-pass","going-in-circles","cursor","codex","founder"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/verify-agent-claims/SKILL.md","name":"verify-agent-claims","description":"Checks whether what a coding agent said it did is true — \"fixed the bug\", \"added tests\", \"all tests pass\", \"removed dead code\", \"no behaviour change\", \"verified\" — by splitting its commits, PR description or chat summary into claims and giving each a verdict (holds, doesn't hold, can't tell) with evidence, written for a founder who doesn't read code. Also unsticks an agent that keeps fixing the same thing. It finds which of two look-alike files is live, dead code kept alive by other dead code, and writes the CLAUDE.md rules that stop the loop. Ships a read-only, self-testing script. Use it whenever someone asks to verify, check or audit what Claude, Cursor, Codex or any AI agent did; says \"did it really fix it\", \"can I trust this PR\", \"it says tests pass\", \"it keeps breaking the same thing\", \"it's going in circles\"; is about to merge AI-written code they can't read; or inherited an AI-built codebase, even if they never say \"verify\".","headings":["Ve